sad breaking news overnight at least 53  people dead more than 100 injured after  a cargo truck crashed in southern mexico  this is a truck said to be carrying  migrants mostly from guatemala and  honduras fleeing crime and poverty there  in search of a better life somewhere  omar villafranca has that story  a horrific scene in southern mexico  about 100 miles from the guatemalan  border authorities say a cargo truck  with some 200 people inside tried to  make a sharp turn rolled over and  crashed into a pedestrian bridge  this man a migrant from guatemala was in  the truck when it crashed he says that  when the truck hit a curb the sheer  weight of everyone inside caused the  vehicle to tip over he says many on  board were migrants from guatemala and  honduras  a rescue worker says a survivor told him  the truck was speeding when it lost  control many are fleeing poverty in  central america worsened by back-to-back  hurricanes as cbs news reported from  guatemala earlier this year  back in april we spoke to this 19 year  old who said he made it all the way to  mexico city before he ran out of money  to pay smugglers the white house is  urging migrants to stay in their  homelands and just reinstated the remain  in mexico policy for asylum seekers but  critics say tougher immigration policies  are what force migrants to rely on  smugglers to make the journey to the u.s  putting their lives at risk for cbs  mornings i'm omar villafranca
 

